Scripts placed in .git/hooks/ (e.g., pre-commit, post-merge) run automatically.
Example pre-commit:

#!/bin/sh
npm test || exit 1

Bonus Section — Professional Git Practices
GitFlow Model

main → production releases

develop → integration branch

feature/ → per-feature work

release/ → stabilization

hotfix/ → urgent production fixes

Commands:

git flow init
git flow feature start login

Trunk-Based Development

Single main branch, small frequent commits, feature flags.
Simpler than GitFlow for CI/CD teams.

Pro Tips

💙 Avoid force-push on shared branches
💙 Always use git revert instead of reset on remote branches
💙 Use signed tags for releases
💙 Run git gc monthly to optimize repositories

Quick Reference Cheat Sheet
Action	Command
Init repo	git init
Clone	git clone url
Stage files	git add .
Commit	git commit -m "msg"
Push	git push origin branch
Fetch updates	git fetch
Pull updates	git pull
Create branch	git checkout -b branch
Merge	git merge branch
Rebase	git rebase branch
Revert commit	git revert sha
Reset commit	git reset --hard sha
View log	git log --oneline --graph
Recover commit	git reflog + git branch name sha
Stash work	git stash / git stash pop
Delete branch	git branch -d branch
Delete remote branch	git push origin --delete branch
Compare branches	git diff main..dev
Find author of line	git blame file
Bisect bug	git bisect start
	
